.TH EGRAPH-BUILD 1 2026-09-29 "egraph @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
egraph-build \- evaluate the installed packages through portage and write egraph's store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B egraph-build
.RB [ \-\-full | \-\-incremental | \-\-evaluate | \-\-json | \-\-evaluated\-json | \-\-repository | \-\-repository\-json | \-\-pending | \-\-kernel\-sources | \-\-emerge\-options | \-\-notices | \-\-worker ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ entry ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B egraph-build
imports portage, read-only, and writes what
.BR egraph (1)
answers from: the installed store (every installed package's dependencies, slots, sonames and the
root sets) and the evaluated store beside it (the dependencies emerge reads, masks, and the
versions each package could move to).
Both are written to temporary files and renamed into place, so readers never see a partial store.
.PP
.B egraph
runs it itself whenever the store no longer describes the system, so it rarely needs running by
hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-full
Evaluate every installed package (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-incremental
Evaluate again only the packages whose inputs changed since the stores were written.
.TP
.B \-\-evaluate
As
.BR \-\-incremental ,
and evaluate each
.IR entry ,
a category/package name with ebuilds in a repository, with what it would pull in.
The evaluated store keeps them through later builds until a
.BR \-\-full
one, or until they are installed.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the installed layer as canonical JSON instead of writing the store.
.TP
.B \-\-evaluated\-json
Print the evaluated layer as canonical JSON instead of writing the store.
.TP
.B \-\-repository
Write the repository index beside the store
.RI ( installed.repository.egraph ):
every version of every package in the repositories, and the configuration that decides which
are visible, as portage parsed it.
Of an index already there, only the packages whose metadata changed are read again, and after a
configuration change only the configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-repository\-json
Print the repository index as canonical JSON instead of writing it.
.TP
.B \-\-pending
Write what each
.I entry
of a merge list
.RB ( ebuild:\fIcpv\fR " or " binary:\fIcpv\fR )
waits for, as JSON, to
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.B \-\-kernel\-sources
Write the directories straight under
.I /usr/src
named
.BI linux\- *
that each
.IR entry ,
an installed cpv, lists in its
.BR CONTENTS ,
as JSON, to
.BR \-\-output ;
.BR egraph (1)
asks before a plan replaces a slot, to keep the running kernel's sources.
.TP
.B \-\-emerge\-options
Write
.B EMERGE_DEFAULT_OPTS
as emerge splits it, the log elog's
.B save_summary
module appends to, and
.B PORTAGE_ELOG_SYSTEM
without
.B echo
when that log holds every class echo shows, and under
.B FEATURES=jobserver\-token
the named pipe of the last
.B \-\-jobserver\-auth
in
.BR MAKEFLAGS ,
which
.B emerge
takes a token from for each build, and
.BR PORTAGE_TMPDIR ,
as JSON, to
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.B \-\-notices
Write the configuration files with updates waiting, as emerge finds them, the unread news
items with their titles, and the preserved libraries with the packages using them and the
atoms of
.BR @preserved\-rebuild ,
as JSON, to
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.B \-\-copy\-portage
Copy the running portage (its bin directory, and its
.B portage
and
.B _emerge
packages) to the directory
.BR \-\-output ,
which must not exist yet, for workers to run from while a run merges a new portage, as
.B emerge
copies itself before it updates itself.
.TP
.B \-\-worker
Build and merge, or uninstall, each package requested on standard input, one JSON object a
line, in turn as
.B emerge
does.
.B {\(dqcpv\(dq: ..., \(dqrepo\(dq: ...}
builds the ebuild from source and merges it, as
.B emerge \-1
does; with
.BR "\(dqblockers\(dq: [" cpv ", ...]" ,
the installed packages it blocks or that block it, whose files it may take over before they
are uninstalled, and with
.BR "\(dqworld\(dq: " atom ,
the atom to record in the world file once it is merged.
.B {\(dqbuild\(dq: ..., \(dqrepo\(dq: ...}
only builds it, and
.B {\(dqmerge\(dq: ...}
(with
.B \(dqblockers\(dq
and
.B \(dqworld\(dq
as above) then merges what that worker built: its build directory stays locked from the one to
the other, as
.B emerge
keeps it while a built package waits its turn to merge; several may wait at once, merged in
any order.
.B {\(dquninstall\(dq: ...}
uninstalls an installed package; with
.BR "\(dqclean_world\(dq: true" ,
the world file's atoms that then match nothing installed go too, as
.B emerge \-C
drops them.
Each request's progress goes to standard output, one JSON object a line:
.B {\(dqphase\(dq: ...}
as each phase starts (a merge's build phases and
.BR merge ,
an uninstall's
.BR unmerge ),
then
.BR {\(dqbuilt\(dq:\ ...} ", " {\(dqmerged\(dq:\ ...} " or " {\(dquninstalled\(dq:\ ...} ,
.B {\(dqfailed\(dq: ..., \(dqstatus\(dq: ..., \(dqlog\(dq: ...}
naming the phase that failed and its build log, or
.B {\(dqerror\(dq: ...}
for a request that cannot be tried. What portage and the ebuild print goes to standard error
and the build log.
.TP
.BI \-\-portage\-copy " dir"
With
.BR \-\-worker :
import portage, and run the ebuilds, from the copy
.B \-\-copy\-portage
made in
.IR dir .
.TP
.B \-\-background
With
.BR \-\-worker ,
what the builds, merges and uninstalls print goes only to their build logs, as
.B emerge
sends it there when it runs more than one job.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " file"
The file
.BR \-\-pending ", " \-\-kernel\-sources ", " \-\-emerge\-options " and " \-\-notices
write, apart from anything portage prints; the directory
.B \-\-copy\-portage
makes.
.TP
.BI \-\-store " file"
The store to write (default
.BR $EGRAPH_STORE ,
else
.IR ${EROOT}/var/cache/egraph/installed.egraph );
the evaluated store goes beside it.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " dir"
The root whose installed packages to evaluate (default
.BR $ROOT ).
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-root " dir"
The root of the portage configuration to evaluate them with (default
.BR $PORTAGE_CONFIGROOT ).
.TP
.BI \-\-eprefix " dir"
The offset prefix of a prefix installation (default
.BR $PORTAGE_OVERRIDE_EPREFIX ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR ROOT ", " PORTAGE_CONFIGROOT ", " PORTAGE_OVERRIDE_EPREFIX ", " EGRAPH_STORE
Defaults for
.BR \-\-root ", " \-\-config\-root ", " \-\-eprefix " and " \-\-store .
.TP
.B EGRAPH_STRICT
When 1, an incremental build is also compared with a full one, and a difference fails it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure.
.TP
.B 2
The command line could not be parsed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR egraph (1),
.BR portage (5)
